IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-companies-domain`

§ `Part 3 — Constitution of Companies`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 3, ss 17–42A.
-- Source: SSO current version as at 07 Sep 2026.
--
-- ENCODING SCOPE. Part 3 is heavily procedural — much of it describes
-- what documents to lodge and what the Registrar must do. This encoding
-- captures the COMPUTABLE rules: eligibility conditions, thresholds,
-- deadlines, and decision logic that an automated system can evaluate.
-- Purely administrative steps (lodge document X, Registrar issues notice Y)
-- are noted in comments but not modelled as rules.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Division 1 — Incorporation`


§§§ `s 17 — Formation of companies`

-- s 17(2): the three types of company that may be formed
-- (modelled as the Company Type enum in the domain)

-- s 17(3): the 20-person limit for unregistered associations
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 17(3)"
GIVEN `number of persons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must register as company` IF
    `number of persons` GREATER THAN 20

-- s 17(5): no guarantee company with share capital after 15 Aug 1984
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 17(5)"
GIVEN `company type`                    IS A `Company Type`
    , `has share capital`               IS A BOOLEAN
    , `registered after 15 August 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guarantee with share capital prohibited` IF
        `company type` EQUALS `company limited by guarantee`
    AND `has share capital`
    AND `registered after 15 August 1984`


§§§ `s 18 — Private company`

-- s 18(1): conditions for incorporation as private company
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 18(1)"
GIVEN c IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be incorporated as private company` IF
        c's `has share capital`
    AND c's `restricts share transfer`
    AND c's `member limit in constitution` AT MOST 50


§§§ `s 19 — Registration and incorporation`

-- s 19(1): requirements for incorporation (procedural — noted, not modelled)
-- The three requirements are:
--   (a) submit constitution and prescribed documents to Registrar
--   (b) furnish last day of first financial year and prescribed info
--   (c) pay prescribed fee

-- s 19(5): effect of incorporation — subscribers become body corporate
-- (declaratory — not modelled)


§§§ `s 20 — Power to refuse registration`

-- s 20(2): mandatory grounds for refusal
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 20(2)"
GIVEN `likely used for unlawful purpose`    IS A BOOLEAN
    , `contrary to national security`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Registrar must refuse registration` IF
        `likely used for unlawful purpose`
    OR  `contrary to national security`

-- s 20(3): appeal period
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 20(3)"
`appeal period for registration refusal` MEANS 30


§§§ `s 20A — Minimum of one member`

@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 20A"
GIVEN c IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets minimum member requirement` IF
    c's `number of members` AT LEAST 1


§§§ `s 21 — Membership of holding company`

-- s 21(1): a subsidiary cannot be a member of its holding company
-- s 21(4)(b): disposal deadline for pre-existing shares
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 21(4)(b)"
`subsidiary share disposal period months` MEANS 12

-- s 21(6E)(a),(b): the 10% aggregate limit on subsidiary-held shares
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 21(6E)"
GIVEN `shares held by subsidiaries` IS A NUMBER
    , `treasury shares`             IS A NUMBER
    , `total shares in class`       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsidiary share limit exceeded` IF
    (`shares held by subsidiaries` PLUS `treasury shares`)
        GREATER THAN (`total shares in class` TIMES 0.1)

-- s 21(6E)(c): disposal period for excess shares
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 21(6E)(c)"
`excess share disposal period months` MEANS 6

-- s 21(6E)(d),(e): dividend restriction based on wholly-owned status
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 21(6E)(d)–(e)"
GIVEN `is wholly owned subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dividend permitted on subsidiary held shares` IF
    NOT `is wholly owned subsidiary`


§§§ `s 22 — Requirements as to constitution`

-- s 22(1): what the constitution must state (procedural — noted, not modelled)
-- Key requirements: company name, liability type, subscriber details

-- s 22(1AB): default penalty for failure to notify member number change
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 22(1AB)"
`penalty for member number notification default` MEANS 2000


§§ `Division 2 — Powers`


§§§ `s 23 — Capacity and powers of company`

-- s 23(1): full capacity subject to Act and constitution (declaratory)
-- s 23(1B): constitution may restrict capacity (declaratory)


§§§ `s 25 — Ultra vires transactions`

-- s 25(1): no act invalid merely for lack of capacity (declaratory)
-- s 25(2): who may assert lack of capacity
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 25(2)"
DECLARE `Ultra Vires Standing` IS ONE OF
    `member restraining company act`
    `holder of floating charge debentures`
    `trustee for debenture holders`
    `company against present or former officers`
    `Minister to wind up`


§§§ `s 25C — Constitutional limitations: transactions with directors`

-- s 25C(3): transaction is voidable if it involves a director or connected person
-- s 25C(5): conditions under which the transaction ceases to be voidable
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 25C(5)"
GIVEN `restitution impossible`          IS A BOOLEAN
    , `company indemnified`             IS A BOOLEAN
    , `bona fide rights would be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `transaction affirmed by company`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `director transaction ceases to be voidable` IF
        `restitution impossible`
    OR  `company indemnified`
    OR  `bona fide rights would be affected`
    OR  `transaction affirmed by company`


§§§ `s 25D — Persons connected with director`

-- s 25D(2)(a): director's family
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 25D(2)(a)"
DECLARE `Family Relationship` IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `son`
    `adopted son`
    `stepson`
    `daughter`
    `adopted daughter`
    `stepdaughter`

-- s 25D(2)(b): connected body corporate — 20% threshold
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 25D(2)(b)"
GIVEN `share capital interest pct`  IS A NUMBER
    , `voting power pct`            IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `director connected with body corporate` IF
        `share capital interest pct` AT LEAST 20
    OR  `voting power pct` GREATER THAN 20


§§§ `s 26 — Alteration of constitution`

-- s 26(1): constitution may be altered by special resolution (procedural)
-- s 26(2): 14-day lodgement deadline after passing resolution
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 26(2)"
`constitution alteration lodgement days` MEANS 14

-- s 26(2A): default penalty
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 26(2A)"
`penalty for alteration lodgement default` MEANS 1000


§§§ `s 26A — Entrenching provisions`

-- s 26A(1)(b): insertion requires unanimous consent
-- s 26A(2): removal or alteration requires unanimous consent
-- s 26A(4): definition of entrenching provision
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 26A(4)"
GIVEN `requires supermajority`           IS A BOOLEAN
    , `supermajority threshold pct`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `valid entrenching provision` IF
    NOT `requires supermajority`
    OR  `supermajority threshold pct` GREATER THAN 75


§§§ `s 27 — Names of companies`

-- s 27(7): "Limited" or "Berhad" required at end of name
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 27(7)"
GIVEN c IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must have Limited or Berhad in name` IF
    c's `company type` EQUALS `company limited by shares`
    OR c's `company type` EQUALS `company limited by guarantee`

-- s 27(8): "Private" or "Sendirian" required before "Limited"/"Berhad"
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 27(8)"
GIVEN c IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must have Private in name` IF
    c's `classification` EQUALS `private company`

-- s 27(12B)(a): name reservation period
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 27(12B)(a)"
`name reservation period days` MEANS 60

-- s 27(12B)(a): extension period
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 27(12B)(a)"
`name reservation extension days` MEANS 60

-- s 27(12C): appeal period for name refusal
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 27(12C)"
`appeal period for name refusal days` MEANS 30

-- s 27(1A): dissolved entity name reuse waiting periods
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 27(1A)"
GIVEN entity IS A `Dissolved Entity`
    , `current date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `name reuse waiting period years` entity `current date` IS
    CONSIDER entity's `entity type`
    WHEN `existing company` THEN
        CONSIDER entity's `dissolution method`
        WHEN `wound up`             THEN 2
        WHEN `struck off register`  THEN 6
        OTHERWISE                        2
    WHEN `limited liability partnership` THEN
        CONSIDER entity's `dissolution method`
        WHEN `wound up`             THEN 2
        WHEN `struck off register`  THEN 6
        OTHERWISE                        2
    WHEN `limited partnership` THEN 1
    WHEN `foreign company` THEN
        CONSIDER entity's `dissolution method`
        WHEN `ceased business`      THEN 0
        WHEN `struck off register`  THEN 6
        OTHERWISE                        2
    WHEN `VCC` THEN
        CONSIDER entity's `dissolution method`
        WHEN `wound up`             THEN 2
        WHEN `struck off register`  THEN 6
        OTHERWISE                        2
    OTHERWISE 2


§§§ `s 28 — Change of name`

-- s 28(6): change of name does not affect identity or obligations (declaratory)

-- s 28(3): direction to change name — 6 weeks to comply
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 28(3)"
`name change compliance weeks` MEANS 6

-- s 28(3B): default penalty for non-compliance
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 28(3B)"
`penalty for name change non compliance` MEANS 2000

-- s 28(3D): appeal periods
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 28(3D)"
`appeal period for name change direction days` MEANS 30


§§§ `s 29 — Omission of Limited or Berhad`

-- s 29(1): conditions for omission (all must be satisfied)
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 29(1)"
GIVEN `purpose is community benefit`   IS A BOOLEAN
    , `has national or public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `financially able`                IS A BOOLEAN
    , `profits applied to objects`      IS A BOOLEAN
    , `prohibits dividend to members`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may omit Limited from name` IF
        `purpose is community benefit`
    AND `has national or public interest`
    AND `financially able`
    AND `profits applied to objects`
    AND `prohibits dividend to members`


§§§ `s 32 — Default in complying with private company requirements`

-- s 32(1): conditions under which private company provisions cease to apply
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 32(1)"
GIVEN c                                               IS A Company
    , `lacks share transfer restriction`              IS A BOOLEAN
    , `lacks member limit`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    , `member limit exceeded`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    , `default not accidental or due to increase`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`private company provisions cease to apply` c `lacks share transfer restriction` `lacks member limit` `member limit exceeded` `default not accidental or due to increase` MEANS
        c's `classification` EQUALS `private company`
    AND (   `lacks share transfer restriction`
         OR `lacks member limit`
         OR (`member limit exceeded` AND `default not accidental or due to increase`))

-- s 32(5): penalty for breach of constitution provisions
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 32(5)"
`penalty for private company constitution breach` MEANS 5000


§§§ `s 33 — Alterations of objects in constitution`

-- s 33(1): 21-day notice before special resolution
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 33(1)"
`notice period for objects alteration days` MEANS 21

-- s 33(2): standing to apply to Court — 5% threshold
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 33(2)"
GIVEN `percentage of issued shares or debentures` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has standing to oppose objects alteration` IF
    `percentage of issued shares or debentures` AT LEAST 5

-- s 33(2): application deadline
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 33(2)"
`deadline to apply to Court for objects alteration days` MEANS 21

-- s 33(5): lodgement deadline after resolution or order
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 33(5)"
`lodgement deadline after resolution or order days` MEANS 14


§§§ `s 38 — Constitution of companies limited by guarantee`

-- s 38(1): void provision — profit distribution to non-members
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 38(1)"
GIVEN `is member`              IS A BOOLEAN
    , `has right to profits`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `void guarantee company profit provision` IF
    NOT `is member` AND `has right to profits`


§§§ `s 39 — Effect of constitution`

-- s 39(3): alteration increasing liability not binding without written consent
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 39(3)"
GIVEN `alteration increases liability`   IS A BOOLEAN
    , `member gave written consent`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liability increase binding on member` IF
    NOT `alteration increases liability`
    OR  `member gave written consent`


§§§ `s 40 — Copies of constitution`

-- s 40(2): maximum charge for copy of constitution
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 40(2)"
`maximum charge for constitution copy` MEANS 5


§§§ `s 41B — Execution of deeds without common seal`

-- s 41B(1): valid signing configurations for executing deeds
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 41B(1)"
GIVEN config IS A `Signing Configuration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `valid deed execution` config IF
    CONSIDER config
    WHEN `director and secretary` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `two directors`          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `director and witness`   THEN TRUE


§§§ `s 42A — Company with charitable purpose contravening Charities Act`

-- s 42A: conditions under which company may be wound up or struck off
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 42A"
GIVEN `is registered charity`          IS A BOOLEAN
    , `has charitable purpose object`  IS A BOOLEAN
    , `convicted under Charities Act`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be wound up for charity contravention` IF
        (`is registered charity` OR `has charitable purpose object`)
    AND `convicted under Charities Act`


-- ===========================================================================
-- TEST CASES
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Part 3 — Illustrations`

-- s 17(3): 20-person limit
`group of 15` MEANS 15
`group of 25` MEANS 25

#ASSERT NOT (`must register as company` `group of 15`)
#ASSERT `must register as company` `group of 25`

-- s 18(1): private company eligibility
`Acme Private` MEANS Company WITH
    `name`                     IS "Acme Pte Ltd"
    `company type`             IS `company limited by shares`
    `classification`           IS `private company`
    `date of incorporation`    IS YMD 2024 1 15
    `has constitution`         IS TRUE
    `has share capital`        IS TRUE
    `number of members`        IS 5
    `member limit in constitution` IS 50
    `restricts share transfer` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `may be incorporated as private company` `Acme Private`

-- s 18(1): company with too many members cannot be private
`Too Many Members Co` MEANS Company WITH
    `name`                     IS "Big Co Pte Ltd"
    `company type`             IS `company limited by shares`
    `classification`           IS `private company`
    `date of incorporation`    IS YMD 2024 6 1
    `has constitution`         IS TRUE
    `has share capital`        IS TRUE
    `number of members`        IS 60
    `member limit in constitution` IS 100
    `restricts share transfer` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT (`may be incorporated as private company` `Too Many Members Co`)

-- s 20A: minimum member requirement
#ASSERT `meets minimum member requirement` `Acme Private`

-- s 21(6E): subsidiary share limit
#ASSERT `subsidiary share limit exceeded` 800 300 10000
#ASSERT NOT (`subsidiary share limit exceeded` 500 300 10000)

-- s 25C(5): when director transaction ceases to be voidable
#ASSERT `director transaction ceases to be voidable` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`director transaction ceases to be voidable` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 25D(2)(b): director connected with body corporate
#ASSERT `director connected with body corporate` 20 10
#ASSERT `director connected with body corporate` 5 25
#ASSERT NOT (`director connected with body corporate` 10 15)

-- s 27(7): Limited in name requirement
#ASSERT `must have Limited or Berhad in name` `Acme Private`
#ASSERT `must have Private in name` `Acme Private`

-- s 29(1): omission of Limited
#ASSERT `may omit Limited from name` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`may omit Limited from name` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- s 33(2): standing to oppose objects alteration
#ASSERT `has standing to oppose objects alteration` 5
#ASSERT `has standing to oppose objects alteration` 10
#ASSERT NOT (`has standing to oppose objects alteration` 3)

-- s 39(3): liability increase binding
#ASSERT `liability increase binding on member` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `liability increase binding on member` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`liability increase binding on member` TRUE FALSE)

-- s 41B: valid deed execution
#ASSERT `valid deed execution` `director and secretary`
#ASSERT `valid deed execution` `two directors`
#ASSERT `valid deed execution` `director and witness`

-- s 42A: charity contravention
#ASSERT `may be wound up for charity contravention` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`may be wound up for charity contravention` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
